feat: installer scripts + improved seed templates

## Summary

Implement one-command installer + standardized seed templates. Users no longer need manual PATH setup or coding—installation is automatic and seeds are self-documenting for all skill levels.

## Changes

### 1. Installer Scripts (NEW)

Add platform-specific installers that auto-detect Go, build binary, and install to GOPATH/bin:

- **install.sh** — Linux, macOS, Git Bash
  * Detects Go version & GOPATH/bin
  * Builds binary
  * Sets executable permission
  * Warns if PATH needs manual setup
  * Works with bash/sh

- **install.bat** — Windows CMD
  * Auto-detects Go & GOPATH/bin
  * Builds with `go build -o dt.exe`
  * Moves binary to %GOPATH%\bin
  * Shows PATH warning if needed
  * Uses native Windows commands (move, where)

- **install.ps1** — Windows PowerShell
  * Full PowerShell implementation
  * Detects GOPATH & creates bin folder if missing
  * Moves binary with Move-Item
  * PATH verification & warning
  * Colored output (✓ Green, ⚠️  Yellow, ❌ Red)

**Result:** User runs one command → binary in PATH → works from any directory after terminal restart.

### 2. Improved Seed Templates (UPDATED)

Standardize all 4 seed docs with consistent format: title + description + sections + command list with explanations. Each command follows:

```
### Command Name
**Deskripsi:** Short explanation (what it does, why use it)
```bash
command examples
```
```

#### git.md
- **Setup** — Initial configuration (user.name, user.email)
- **Daily Workflow** — status, add, commit, pull --rebase, push
- **Branch** — switch -c, switch, branch -d
- **Undo / Fix** — restore --staged, restore, reset --soft, reset --hard, revert
- **View History** — log, diff, show
- **Remote** — clone, remote, fetch
- **Tips** — Best practices (commit often, rebase before push, backup branch)

#### npm.md
- **Setup** — npm init, npm install
- **Install Packages** — npm install, npm install -D, npm uninstall
- **Run Scripts** — npm run, npm run with args, npm exec / npx
- **Publish / Version** — npm version, npm publish
- **Info** — npm list, npm view, npm outdated
- **Global** — npm install -g, npm list -g
- **Troubleshooting** — cache clean, npm audit, rm node_modules + reinstall

#### yarn.md
- **Setup** — yarn init, yarn install
- **Install Packages** — yarn add, yarn add -D, yarn remove
- **Run Scripts** — yarn run, yarn [SCRIPT], yarn with args
- **Info** — yarn list, yarn why
- **Global** — yarn global add, yarn global list
- **Upgrade / Update** — yarn up, yarn upgrade
- **Workspaces** — yarn workspaces list, yarn workspace WORKSPACE add
- **Troubleshooting** — cache clean, autoclean, reinstall

#### pnpm.md
- **Setup** — pnpm init, pnpm install
- **Install Packages** — pnpm add, pnpm add -D, pnpm remove
- **Run Scripts** — pnpm run, pnpm [SCRIPT], pnpm with args
- **Info** — pnpm list, pnpm why, pnpm store
- **Global** — pnpm add -g, pnpm list -g
- **Update / Upgrade** — pnpm up
- **Monorepo** — pnpm recursive, pnpm filter
- **Troubleshooting** — prune, store prune, reinstall

**Format benefits:**
- Juniors: Descriptions + examples + tips (learn context)
- Seniors: Quick reference + organized sections (fast lookup)
- Mixed team: Self-documenting, no confusion on command usage

### 3. Updated README.md (UPDATED)

- **Install section:** 3 clear paths
  * Windows (Git Bash / CMD) — `bash install.sh` or `install.bat`
  * Linux / macOS — `bash install.sh`
  * Manual — `go build -o dt .` + copy to PATH
  
- **New PATH troubleshooting** — Warn if $GOPATH/bin not in PATH, show fix
- **Updated repo layout** — Include install.sh, install.bat, install.ps1
- **Clarified storage & develop sections** — More specific instructions

## Testing

✅ Build: `go build -o dt.exe .` → 14.5 MB binary
✅ Seeds: Auto-load on first run (git.md 3.1KB, npm.md 3.0KB, etc.)
✅ Commands work: `dt list`, `dt show git`, `dt add myguide`
✅ Installer: `bash install.sh` → binary to PATH ✓
✅ CLI from any directory: `dt list` (works from C:\ after PATH set)

## User Impact

**Before:**
- Clone repo
- Manual `go build -o dt.exe .`
- Manual copy binary to PATH folder
- Manual add PATH to environment variables
- Restart terminal 2-3 times
- Seeds are minimal (just code blocks, no explanations)

**After:**
- Clone repo
- Run `bash install.sh` (or `install.bat` / `install.ps1`)
- Restart terminal once
- Done! `dt` works everywhere
- Seeds are complete cheat sheets (command + description + examples + tips)
- Readable for juniors & seniors

## Files Changed

```
NEW:
  install.sh              Installer for Linux/macOS/Git Bash
  install.bat             Installer for Windows CMD
  install.ps1             Installer for Windows PowerShell

UPDATED:
  seeds/git.md            Full git guide (1.2KB → 3.1KB, added deskripsi & organization)
  seeds/npm.md            npm complete guide (259B → 3.0KB)
  seeds/yarn.md           Yarn complete guide (342B → 2.6KB)
  seeds/pnpm.md           pnpm complete guide (284B → 2.6KB)
  README.md               Added install section, PATH troubleshooting, updated layout
```

## Breaking Changes

None. Existing functionality unchanged:
- CLI commands: `dt list`, `dt show`, `dt add`, `dt edit`, `dt delete` still work
- TUI: Menu, list, view, add, edit, delete all unchanged
- Storage: `~/.docxterminal/*.md` location unchanged
- Editor detection: `$EDITOR` → `$VISUAL` → `vim` → `nano` → `notepad` unchanged

